            "content": [
              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following transformation rules:\n- The background color is 7.\n- Any pixel not located at the four corners of the grid remains unchanged.\n- If a pixel of color $C$ is at a corner:\n  - **Top-Left (0, 0)**: Transforms into a $2 \\times 2$ block of color $C$ at rows 1\u20132, columns 1\u20132: `[(1,1), (1,2), (2,1), (2,2)]`.\n  - **Top-Right (0, 7)**: Transforms into a $2 \\times 2$ block of color $C$ at rows 1\u20132, columns 5\u20136: `[(1,5), (1,6), (2,5), (2,6)]`.\n  - **Bottom-Left (7, 0)**: Transforms into 3 pixels of color $C$ at `[(4,2), (5,2), (6,3)]`.\n  - **Bottom-Right (7, 7)**: Transforms into 3 pixels of color $C$ at `[(4,5), (5,5), (6,4)]`.\n  - The original corner pixel itself becomes 7 (the background).\n\nPlease provide the test input grid!",
